! mcp_bootstrap_p110.strap -- printed page 110:
! "********INTERRUPT TABLE**********".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.117, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID
! DB000001  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 110".
!
! FORTY-EIGHT LINES, counted off the page's own printed line-number
! column, 1 to 48 with no gap; below line 48 the page is blank.
!   lines 1-4   comment cards (no LOCATION, no BINARY)
!   line  5     SLC,$      -- prints a LOCATION (215023.00) and a "*"
!   line  6     CNOP       -- prints NOTHING: already word-aligned
!   lines 7-48  42 half-word instructions, 215023.00 .. 215047.40
!
! >>> WHAT THE PAGE IS. <<<  It is the MCP INTERRUPT TABLE: twenty-one
! consecutive WORDS, each holding two half-word instructions, a
! "SIC,<save cell>" in the left half and a "BD,<handler>" in the right.
! Every word is one interrupt-table entry; the entry stores the
! interrupted instruction counter and branches, disabled, to the
! handler.  The one entry that does nothing is word 215041 (lines 35
! and 36), which is NOP / NOP.
!
! THE ADDRESS CHAIN CLOSES END TO END.  Line 7 prints 215023.00, line
! 48 prints 215047.40, and every row is a half word: 42 half words =
! 21 words = 215023.00 .. 215047.40 inclusive, with no gap and no
! overlap.  The deck's SLC puts the first row at 215023.00 and the
! assembler lands line 48 on 215047.40 (see the !CHECK block).
!
! >>> THE PAGE JOINS printed p.103 BY NAME AND BY ADDRESS. <<<
! Line 7 is the only NAMED row on the page and its name is S IT.
! printed p.103 line 47 prints "S IA  VF,SIT" with the resolved value
! 215023.00+, and THIS page prints S IT's LOCATION as 215023.00.  Two
! pages, two independent prints, same address.  That is also why the
! SLC below is written (8)215023. rather than copied from p.103: p.103
! ends at 215021.00 and printed pp.104-109 are not transcribed yet, so
! the two words between 215021.00 and 215023.00 are accounted for by
! THIS page's own printed LOCATION column and by p.103's S IA, not by
! a chain this deck can assemble.
!
! >>> TAIL SCOPE, NOT A COLLISION. <<<  printed p.99 line 11's
! "SLC,(8)215000." moved the origin to 0o215000 and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE
! the TAIL,(2)G block that printed p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37
! closed with UNTAIL,(2).  Names here may legitimately repeat names
! defined in pp.2-98 at different addresses.  Nothing on this page is
! "fixed" on that account.  (SIFDMP is an example already in the tree:
! p.34 SYNs it to 2161.0, p.37 defines it at 002155.00, p.103 defines
! it again at 215011.00.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! HOW THE EXTERNAL ADDRESSES BELOW WERE OBTAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every operand on this page is a symbol defined somewhere else, so
! the SYN values below are BACK-DERIVED FROM THIS PAGE'S OWN BINARY
! OUTPUT COLUMN.  That makes the !CHECK rows a check of the OPCODE
! and MODIFIER bits and of the ADDRESS PLACEMENT, not an independent
! check of the addresses themselves -- listing_oracle.py's docstring
! says exactly this about rows whose operand is external.  What IS
! independent here is the SEVEN-WAY agreement on S IPT:
!
!   line 16  BD,SIPT+4.0   -> 215107.04      215103 + 4  = 215107
!   line 26  BD,SIPT+9.0   -> 215114.04      215103 + 11 = 215114
!   line 28  BD,SIPT+10.0  -> 215115.04      215103 + 12 = 215115
!   line 30  BD,SIPT+11.0  -> 215116.04      215103 + 13 = 215116
!   line 32  BD,SIPT+12.0  -> 215117.04      215103 + 14 = 215117
!   line 34  BD,SIPT+13.0  -> 215120.04      215103 + 15 = 215120
!   line 44  BD,SIPT+18.   -> 215125.04      215103 + 22 = 215125
!   line 48  BD,SIPT+20.   -> 215127.04      215103 + 24 = 215127
!
! (left side decimal, right side octal).  Eight rows, one value,
! S IPT = 215103.00, and the page never prints that address itself.
! A single misread digit in any one of the eight would break it.
!
! >>> AND THE EIGHT OFFSETS ARE THE ENTRIES' OWN INDICES. <<<  This is
! a stronger statement than the one above and it uses NONE of the
! binary column.  Subtract the table's base word 215023 from each of
! those rows' own printed LOCATION and the remainder, read in octal,
! IS the decimal offset the STATEMENT column prints:
!
!   line  LOCATION   loc-215023      statement
!    16   215027.40    4  = 4        BD,SIPT+4.0
!    26   215034.40   11o = 9        BD,S IPT+9.0
!    28   215035.40   12o = 10       BD,S IPT+10.0
!    30   215036.40   13o = 11       BD,S IPT+11.0
!    32   215037.40   14o = 12       BD,S IPT+12.0
!    34   215040.40   15o = 13       BD,S IPT+13.0
!    44   215045.40   22o = 18       BD,SIPT+18.
!    48   215047.40   24o = 20       BD,SIPT+20.
!
! Eight for eight.  Each entry of the table branches to the S IPT cell
! WITH ITS OWN INDEX, so the LOCATION digits, the decimal offsets in
! the STATEMENT column and S IPT's base all cross-check one another
! through printed numbers alone.  THAT IS AN ARITHMETIC INVARIANT
! AMONG PRINTED NUMBERS AND NOTHING MORE -- no claim is made here
! about what S IPT is or what the entries mean.
!
! >>> THE TWELVE Y FX* ADDRESSES RUN STRIDE 2, MONOTONE, IN TABLE
! ORDER. <<<  In the order the table branches to them:
!   216374 216376 216400 216402 216404 | 216430 216432 216434 216436
!   216440 216442 216444
! -- two octal runs, step 2 throughout (376+2 = 400 and 436+2 = 440
! are the two places that look like breaks and are not), increasing in
! exactly the order lines 8, 10, 12, 14, 18, 20, 22, 24, 38, 40, 42
! and 46 appear.  Two words apiece.  This is EVIDENCE AND NOT PROOF --
! a misread digit that happened to land on another stride-2 slot would
! survive it -- but a misread digit that did not would break either
! the stride or the ordering, so ten of the twelve are corroborated by
! their neighbours rather than resting on ink alone.  Note that the
! 216404 -> 216430 gap is NOT all handler stubs: Y MFIC sits inside it
! at 216411.40.
!
! >>> WHY A BD PRINTS ".04" AND A SIC PRINTS THE REAL BIT OFFSET. <<<
! fmt_half in strap/listing_oracle.py prints bits 0-17 as the octal
! word, bits 18-23 as two octal digits and bits 24-31 as the hex byte.
! For a branch, bit 18 is the HALF-WORD SELECT and bits 19-23 belong
! to the operation, so an unconditional BD to a word boundary prints
! ".04" (0o04 = 000100: bit 18 = 0, the op bits = 4) and the same
! branch to the right half word would print ".44".  Every BD on this
! page prints ".04", so every handler address is a WORD boundary.
! printed p.103 line 43 is the control: "BD,SDISIC+.32" with SDISIC at
! 217451.40 resolves to word 217452 bit 0 and prints "217452.04 00" --
! the ".32" in the statement is nowhere in the ".04".  SIC is a
! different format: its printed ".40"/".00" IS the operand's own bit
! offset, which is why Y MFIC is 216411.40 (a right half word) while
! Y SFIC and S T IC are 216604.00 and 215265.00 (left half words).
! Confirmed by assembling, not by reasoning: the smoke test
! "SIC,YMFIC / BD,YFXMK / BD,SIPT+4.0 / NOP" reproduces
! "216411.40 80", "216374.04 00", "215107.04 00", "000000.30 00"
! character for character.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS SETTLED AT 1800-4500 dpi
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This drum opens round glyphs, so an observed C may be a damaged 0/O
! while an observed 0/O is never a damaged C.  The discriminator used
! throughout is the LEFT SIDE: C and O are round with no stem, D has a
! straight vertical left stem and squared corners.  The "BD," at the
! head of twenty-one rows is a free, in-row D specimen for every one
! of them.
!
!   line 18  BD,Y FXCPU   C -- round, wide gap at the right, nothing
!                             like the D two characters to its left.
!   line 24  BD,Y FXCBJ   C -- same.
!   line 38  BD,Y FXOP    O -- CLOSED and round on the left; this is
!                             the one that is NOT a C.  Checked
!                             against line 18's C and line 40's D in
!                             one montage at 1800 dpi x 2.5.
!   line 40  BD,Y FXAD    D -- straight left stem, squared corners.
!   line 46  BD,Y FXDS    D -- straight left stem, squared corners.
!   lines 7+ SIC,Y MFIC   C -- final letter round and open; the same
!                             shape as the C in the mnemonic SIC in
!                             its own row.
!
! THE PAGE CALIBRATES ITSELF ON O/C IN ONE PLACE, AND IT IS WORTH
! RECORDING: lines 35 and 36 are the SAME instruction (both print
! 000000.30 00, which is what CNOP prints on printed p.103 line 48),
! and line 35 prints "NCP" while line 36 prints "NOP".  One drum, two
! adjacent rows, one letter, printed both ways.  Both are NOP.
!
! THE COMMENT COLUMN, used as the English oracle on six rows:
!   line 16  "- TIME SIGNAL INTERRUPT"
!   line 26  "-EPCK INTERRUPT"     (C, not G: no crossbar at 1800 dpi)
!   line 28  "-UK INTERRUPT"
!   line 30  "-EE INTERRUPT"
!   line 32  "-EOP INTERRUPT"      (O: closed, beside line 34's open C)
!   line 34  "-CS INTERRUPT"
! These are IBM's own words for six of the twenty-one entries.  They
! are recorded; NO MEANING IS INFERRED FROM THEM and no symbol on this
! page was spelled from them.
!
! BLANKS INSIDE A NAME ARE NOT CHARACTERS.  The page prints the same
! symbol both ways in the STATEMENT column -- "SIC,STIC" on line 15,
! "SIC,S T IC" on lines 25-33 and "SIC,ST IC" on lines 43 and 47; and
! "BD,SIPT+4.0" on line 16 against "BD,S IPT+9.0" on line 26.  They
! are one symbol each (S T IC = 215265.00, S IPT = 215103.00): the
! binary column prints the SAME address for all of them, which is the
! proof, not the typography.  The deck writes them closed up.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 5 IS PRINTED "SLC,$" AND IS WRITTEN "SLC,(8)215023." HERE.
! "$" is the location counter, so on the real tape line 5 is a no-op
! that re-states where the assembler already is; in a STANDALONE deck
! it would set the origin to 0.  The printed form is kept in the
! listing block below.  strap_asm does accept "SLC,$" -- the
! substitution is for standalone assembly, not for an assembler gap.
!
! NOTHING UNDER strap/, tests/, decks/ OR docs/ WAS MODIFIED.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- every one back-derived from this page's BINARY column
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
YMFIC   SYN, (8)216411.40            ! lines 7,9,11,13,17  SIC operand
YSFIC   SYN, (8)216604.0             ! lines 19,21,23,37,39,41,45
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0             ! lines 15,25,27,29,31,33,43,47
SIPT    SYN, (8)215103.0             ! eight rows agree; see above
YFXMK   SYN, (8)216374.0             ! line 8
YFXIK   SYN, (8)216376.0             ! line 10
YFXIJ   SYN, (8)216400.0             ! line 12
YFXEK   SYN, (8)216402.0             ! line 14
YFXCPU  SYN, (8)216404.0             ! line 18
YFXEKJ  SYN, (8)216430.0             ! line 20
YFXUNR  SYN, (8)216432.0             ! line 22
YFXCBJ  SYN, (8)216434.0             ! line 24
YFXOP   SYN, (8)216436.0             ! line 38
YFXAD   SYN, (8)216440.0             ! line 40
YFXUSA  SYN, (8)216442.0             ! line 42
YFXDS   SYN, (8)216444.0             ! line 46

        SLC, (8)215023.              ! line 5, printed "SLC,$"
        CNOP                         ! line 6, prints no binary
SIT     SIC, YMFIC                   ! line 7
        BD, YFXMK                    ! line 8
        SIC, YMFIC                   ! line 9
        BD, YFXIK                    ! line 10
        SIC, YMFIC                   ! line 11
        BD, YFXIJ                    ! line 12
        SIC, YMFIC                   ! line 13
        BD, YFXEK                    ! line 14
        SIC, STIC                    ! line 15
        BD, SIPT+4.0                 ! line 16 - TIME SIGNAL INTERRUPT
        SIC, YMFIC                   ! line 17
        BD, YFXCPU                   ! line 18
        SIC, YSFIC                   ! line 19
        BD, YFXEKJ                   ! line 20
        SIC, YSFIC                   ! line 21
        BD, YFXUNR                   ! line 22
        SIC, YSFIC                   ! line 23
        BD, YFXCBJ                   ! line 24
        SIC, STIC                    ! line 25
        BD, SIPT+9.0                 ! line 26 -EPCK INTERRUPT
        SIC, STIC                    ! line 27
        BD, SIPT+10.0                ! line 28 -UK INTERRUPT
        SIC, STIC                    ! line 29
        BD, SIPT+11.0                ! line 30 -EE INTERRUPT
        SIC, STIC                    ! line 31
        BD, SIPT+12.0                ! line 32 -EOP INTERRUPT
        SIC, STIC                    ! line 33
        BD, SIPT+13.0                ! line 34 -CS INTERRUPT
        NOP                          ! line 35, printed "NCP"
        NOP                          ! line 36
        SIC, YSFIC                   ! line 37
        BD, YFXOP                    ! line 38
        SIC, YSFIC                   ! line 39
        BD, YFXAD                    ! line 40
        SIC, YSFIC                   ! line 41
        BD, YFXUSA                   ! line 42
        SIC, STIC                    ! line 43
        BD, SIPT+18.                 ! line 44
        SIC, YSFIC                   ! line 45
        BD, YFXDS                    ! line 46
        SIC, STIC                    ! line 47
        BD, SIPT+20.                 ! line 48

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, transcribed from PDF p.117
! LINE  LOCATION    BINARY OUTPUT   NAME   STATEMENT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  1  (comment card)  *********************************************
!   line  2  (comment card)  ********INTERRUPT TABLE**********
!   line  3  (comment card)  *********************************************
!   line  4  (comment card)  (blank text)
!   line  5  215023.00 *  (no binary)                 SLC,$
!   line  6  (no location) (no binary)                CNOP
!   line  7  215023.00   216411.40 80      S IT       SIC,YMFIC
!   line  8  215023.40   216374.04 00                 BD,YFXMK
!   line  9  215024.00   216411.40 80                 SIC,YMFIC
!   line 10  215024.40   216376.04 00                 BD,YFXIK
!   line 11  215025.00   216411.40 80                 SIC,YMFIC
!   line 12  215025.40   216400.04 00                 BD,YFXIJ
!   line 13  215026.00   216411.40 80                 SIC,YMFIC
!   line 14  215026.40   216402.04 00                 BD,YFXEK
!   line 15  215027.00   215265.00 80                 SIC,STIC
!   line 16  215027.40   215107.04 00                 BD,SIPT+4.0   - TIME SIGNAL INTERRUPT
!   line 17  215030.00   216411.40 80                 SIC,YMFIC
!   line 18  215030.40   216404.04 00                 BD,YFXCPU
!   line 19  215031.00   216604.00 80                 SIC,YSFIC
!   line 20  215031.40   216430.04 00                 BD,YFXEKJ
!   line 21  215032.00   216604.00 80                 SIC,YSFIC
!   line 22  215032.40   216432.04 00                 BD,YFXUNR
!   line 23  215033.00   216604.00 80                 SIC,YSFIC
!   line 24  215033.40   216434.04 00                 BD,YFXCBJ
!   line 25  215034.00   215265.00 80                 SIC,S T IC
!   line 26  215034.40   215114.04 00                 BD,S IPT+9.0  -EPCK INTERRUPT
!   line 27  215035.00   215265.00 80                 SIC,S T IC
!   line 28  215035.40   215115.04 00                 BD,S IPT+10.0 -UK INTERRUPT
!   line 29  215036.00 *  215265.00 80                SIC,S T IC
!   line 30  215036.40   215116.04 00                 BD,S IPT+11.0 -EE INTERRUPT
!   line 31  215037.00   215265.00 80                 SIC,S T IC
!   line 32  215037.40   215117.04 00                 BD,S IPT+12.0 -EOP INTERRUPT
!   line 33  215040.00   215265.00 80                 SIC,S T IC
!   line 34  215040.40   215120.04 00                 BD,S IPT+13.0 -CS INTERRUPT
!   line 35  215041.00   000000.30 00                 NOP   (printed "NCP")
!   line 36  215041.40   000000.30 00                 NOP
!   line 37  215042.00   216604.00 80                 SIC,YSFIC
!   line 38  215042.40   216436.04 00                 BD,YFXOP
!   line 39  215043.00   216604.00 80                 SIC,YSFIC
!   line 40  215043.40   216440.04 00                 BD,YFXAD
!   line 41  215044.00   216604.00 80                 SIC,YSFIC
!   line 42  215044.40   216442.04 00                 BD,YFXUSA
!   line 43  215045.00   215265.00 80                 SIC,ST IC
!   line 44  215045.40   215125.04 00                 BD,SIPT+18.
!   line 45  215046.00   216604.00 80                 SIC,YSFIC
!   line 46  215046.40   216444.04 00                 BD,YFXDS
